  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "sanitize",
    "file": "harfbuzz/src/hb-ot-kern-table.hh",
    "description": "OT::kern::sanitize validates only the 2-byte u.major field and, for any unrecognized major version, returns true without ensuring that the 4-byte u.version32 field is present. The accepted truncated blob is stored by kern::accelerator_t; OT::kern::has_data then evaluates u.version32 != 0 and BEInt<uint32_t,4> reads two bytes beyond the heap allocation. The root cause is the permissive default branch / insufficient minimum-size validation in OT::kern::sanitize, rather than the generic BEInt read where ASan reports the crash.",
    "conditions": "A crafted sfnt must expose a kern table blob that is at least 2 bytes but shorter than 4 bytes, with its first two bytes encoding a major version other than 0 or 1. In this PoV, the table directory points kern to offset 0x1a near the end of the 28-byte input, leaving two 0x20 bytes; the oversized declared table length is clipped to the available input. hb_shape initializes the kern accelerator, sanitization accepts major 0x2020 via the default branch, and shape-plan kerning detection calls has_data(), causing the out-of-bounds 4-byte version read."
  },
